@image html nane_logo.png "" width=800px

<strong>A modern C++23 scientific computing library.</strong>

Nane is focused on clear and practical implementations of numerical methods.
The goal is to keep algorithms close to their mathematical definitions while
providing simple and composable interfaces.

## Design

Nane favors small, readable implementations, transparent numerical behavior,
and minimal abstraction around the underlying mathematics.

The library is intended both for scientific computing and for studying how
numerical methods are implemented.

## Start here

New to Nane? Begin with @ref getting_started "Getting Started", then continue
with @ref cmake_integration "Using Nane with CMake" or the numerical tutorials.

